codex
Found defects:

- **Instrument reading a different copy than the one being changed: name vs binding.** Line 424. Exact input: `app_id="arni-hfref"` with `ssot/arni-hfref/arni-hfref.json` as `{"inputs":{"trials":[{"nct":"NCT02468232","by_outcome":{"cvdeath_or_hfh_first":{"slot":"first"}}},{"nct":"NCT02468232","by_outcome":{"cvdeath_or_hfh_first":{"slot":"second"}}}]}}`. Consequence: the second duplicate silently overwrites the first in `by_nct`, so only the last same-NCT trial is modified and the other real cell is left unchanged.

- **Selector keyed to a form the corpus does not use.** Line 333. Exact input: `app_id="alirocumab-lipid"` with all six listed alirocumab NCTs present and each containing `by_outcome.ldlc_pct_change_wk24`. Consequence: for `NCT01507831`, the record says the LDL-C endpoint is `SECONDARY` on lines 328-332, but line 333 stores `_CTG`, i.e. `protocolSection.outcomesModule.primaryOutcomes[0].measure`, pointing audit provenance at the primary-outcome path that the record itself says is the wrong form.

No proven defect found in the pasted file for: check that cannot fail; probe keyed to string a fix removes; idempotency guard satisfied by own comment/marker; CRLF-vs-LF text comparison; merged-cell/off-by-one tabulation/count; zero conflated with absent; negation dropped; wrapper status code reported instead of work.
